## Reviewer got wrong, or a suggestion the checker cannot take

- a#7 suggested a label with no digit. The Korean source link is "영업세법 제10조", so the number checker requires a 10 in the translation. The false statute name is gone; "(10)" stays on the corrected withholding-rule label. URL still flno=3.
- a#5 is a real readability point (M is opaque), and it is also a pinned product string. Not applied.
- a#27's ၂၀၂၃ would be a new number. The reader problem is real; the fix is the ROC gloss (民國), not a Gregorian year.
- a#19 and b#19 are right that the zero-width lines are not Burmese prose. They are also a byte-level match to the Korean source, and the checker fails if the count changes. Not deleted.
- 008's forced letter was already "[အမည်]", not OOO. Nothing to change.
